      "situation": "Dispatch has recovered. The recovery check ran four looks, and the last two at 46 s were clean in a row.",
      "background": "The operator deployed dispatcher 2.1 to 2.2 about 30 s before the symptoms began. Alerts then stopped reaching units on the primary alerting path, and a backlog of 16 items built up with the oldest at 23 s.",
      "assessment": "There were two causes: the alerting primary refused station alerts, failing 89% of calls, and the dispatcher 2.2 release kept missing unit acknowledgements even after the alerting failover. The incident commander failed alerting over to its standby, which succeeded, and then rolled dispatcher back from 2.2 to 2.1, which also succeeded.",
      "recommendation": "Find out why the alerting primary refused deliveries before moving traffic back to it. Hold dispatcher 2.2 until its acknowledgement fault is understood. The operations team should review the 16 backlogged assignments, including 75, 213 and 214, to confirm every unit was alerted and acknowledged."
    },
